    <div>
      <h3>#141 does supersede #138, as its author claimed <span class="verdict v-clear">verified</span></h3>
      <p>PR #141's description asserts that the ADOPT-0a/0b evidence from #138 was reconciled into it. That checks out: commit <code>096213e</code> ("docs: reconcile ADOPT live evidence with RC baseline") is on the branch, and <code>docs/qa/ADOPT_0AB_LIVE_VERIFICATION_2026-07-17.md</code> is present in its tree. <code>STATE.md</code> and <code>BACKLOG.md</code> differ from #138's versions because #141 carries them further.</p>
      <p class="meta">#138 can be closed as superseded once #141 lands. It does not need to be merged first.</p>
    </div>
